or's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"The script's two self-skips (`no GNU find`, `find lacks -printf`) call base-test.sh `pass` (not `skip`) and exit 0. The JUnit testcase would therefore record a pass with nothing run. On this run the evidence points to a real run. `menu-file-test.sh` sits in the same suite behind a GNU find -printf gate that records a JUnit skip (proof.yaml:200), and it ran and passed: testResults show 56/56 passed, 0 skipped. Its new witness rows independently exercise FFTQ and 9H5Y. Upstream could use `skip` (`# SKIP`), which test/junit/live-session.sh already treats as a skip.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-file-symlink-root-test.sh","kind":"file","line":11},{"id":"proof.yaml","kind":"file","line":200},{"id":"test/junit/live-session.sh","kind":"file","line":129}],"severity":"info","title":"The PR's test passes on a self-skip too (opinion)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"The body still says 'Dedup rows after `cut -f2-` with `awk '!seen[$0]++'`'. Head 03e6af6 keys on `%D:%i` before `cut -f3-`. Worth updating so the merged history describes the shipped mechanism, including the hard-link consequence.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-file","kind":"file","line":52}],"severity":"info","title":"PR description no longer matches the head (opinion)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"`-printf` was already GNU-only, and `%D`/`%i` are also GNU (both test scripts gate on GNU find). The `checks_skipped` disclosure (13 gates, e.g. documentation_coverage, security_surface_covered) is configuration, not caused by this PR. Any external auditor assessment recorded on this package is advisory: a note, not an approval.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-file-symlink-root-test.sh","kind":"file","line":10},{"id":"documentation_coverage","kind":"check"}],"severity":"info","title":"Pre-existing: GNU find dependency; 13 checks skipped by configuration","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"The package's subject head is 03e6af6a (evaluated tree 697ae179). On 2026-10-03 upstream pushed cc710e11, 'Keep hard-linked names apart in the menu-file dedup'. It changes the awk key from device:inode to device:inode plus the file's base name, and adds a symlink-root test row where two hard links with different names in one root give two rows. Its commit message says aliased roots still collapse because the name is the same. None of this is in the package: readiness, test results and the requirement cells above describe 03e6af6a. 9H5Y's title states that the picker identifies a file by device and inode, so a package for cc710e11 must re-check 9H5Y and its witnesses. This review does not assess cc710e11's code.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-file","kind":"file","line":55},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-9H5Y","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"The evidence is for head 03e6af6a; upstream head cc710e11 is not evaluated","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Our proof work added `refuse()` to `menu-file-test.sh` (d15ee632) and traced it (6602a34e) with `# Verifies: SW-REQ-260922-HR29, SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ, SW-REQ-261002-9H5Y` on line 120. review.scope lists it as an added unit with a function-level mapping and no flags. It runs the real script, asserts exit 1, the `Path not found` message, and that the selector is never reached. It is called for a missing path (HR29, line 131 tag), a link root whose target is gone (FFTQ, line 137) and a missing path next to a real root (9H5Y, line 141); these rows are the error_handling witnesses behind the three `observed_pass` cells.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-file-test.sh","kind":"file","line":121},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-HR29","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-9H5Y","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"The new refuse() test helper is traced at function level to all three requirements","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:e1ab91128a45dda9bff9bba4ffd1a97da20da8ebc976241aa4f1e333220bc06f","packageIdentity":"epkg-2b41d5e0a1abb814d6823d088f51b54b7b462f935aae8fa40dcb99956829cad9","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"A small, well-motivated pipeline change, evaluated at head 03e6af6a only (upstream head cc710e11 is not evaluated). Its purpose is now codified (FFTQ, 9H5Y) and observed passing, with witnesses that fail on the base. Coverage of the script was not measured, effects were not analyzed, and the differential harness does not run the script. Untested edges remain: hard-link collapse, pipefail exit 1 via an unreadable directory under a followed root (named open in FFTQ), tie order and alias spelling, symlink-to-file roots."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":4,"rationale":"Settles whether %D:%i dedup should drop a distinct, selectable path; record the decision in 9H5Y or the code.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-file","kind":"file","line":55}],"title":"Hard-linked files under one root"},{"forClaim":5,"rationale":"mkdir a mode-000 dir under the link target (run as non-root), pick a file with a stub selector, and assert omarchy-menu-file's exit status (and omarchy-transcode's).","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-file","kind":"file","line":54},{"id":"bin/omarchy-transcode","kind":"file","line":169}],"title":"Unreadable subdirectory under a followed symlink root"},{"forClaim":6,"rationale":"touch -d the same time on two files and on an aliased pair, then assert row order and which path the stub selector receives, at base and head.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-file","kind":"file","line":55}],"title":"Equal-mtime ordering and surviving alias spelling"},{"forClaim":7,"rationale":"Pass a symlink to a matching file as the path argument; assert whether it is offered.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-file","kind":"file","line":54}],"title":"Symlink-to-file root"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #13197 (Bartok9, part of #12665) makes `bin/omarchy-menu-file` list files under symlinked roots, so `omarchy transcode` gets a picker when `~/Videos` is a link. It runs `find -H` (start points followed, links inside a root not descended), prints `%D:%i`, and keeps one row per device:inode after the mtime sort. It adds `test/shell.d/menu-file-symlink-root-test.sh` (8 rows). The evaluated tree 697ae179 is baseline quattro-proof 39746e65 plus the upstream change at head 03e6af6a (fa7b9387) plus our proof work (2c4063db..6602a34e): SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ and -9H5Y, witnesses in `menu-file-test.sh`, reviews REVIEW-261002-6P46/-VZ1K. **This evidence is for 03e6af6a only.** Upstream pushed cc710e11 on 2026-10-03 (dedup key becomes device:inode plus file name); it is not evaluated here. The PR body still describes a path-string dedup.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** The package says readiness `ready`; next decision `human_judgement` (acceptance) by a maintainer. Disclosures: 3, all inform (coverage_unmeasured, checks_skipped, effects_unavailable). FFTQ, 9H5Y and HR29 are `observed_pass`, with error_handling cells `observed_pass`; HR29's external_call_timeout_bounded is `not_linked` (accepted KI debt). testResults: 56 passed, 0 failed, current. Coverage of the